Patch 1/2 already carries Yixun Lan's Reviewed-by and the FIELD_PREP() fix
for clrsetbits_le32(addr, PAD_DRIVE, ds) is a real bug fix - previously `ds`
was written unshifted into PAD_DRIVE's bit position, which would corrupt the
register unless PAD_DRIVE happened to start at bit 0. Good catch.

One thing worth double-checking: spacemit_pinmux_property_set() now returns
`pin` instead of 0 on success:

  ret = spacemit_pinmux_set(dev, pin, mux);
  if (ret < 0)
          return ret;
  return pin;

Is this return value actually consumed by a caller that needs the pin
number (e.g. for group-apply ordering), or just conventionally expected to
be "last successful pin" similar to some pinctrl frameworks? If no caller
inspects it, returning pin instead of 0 is harmless but worth a comment
explaining why.

Patch 2/2 (IO power domain configuration support) - wasn't fully visible in
this review pass; please confirm it doesn't regress the io_type handling
touched here, since both patches modify the same io_pins[] external-pin
logic (priv->io_pins[i].io_type != IO_TYPE_EXTERNAL check).
